# SentinelNet Workspace Rules for Cline

## Communication Style
- Keep responses concise and focused.
- Drop filler words and unnecessary preambles/postampling.
- Direct execution first; explain only when requested.

## Code Quality & Verification (Mandatory before completion)
Run the following verification checks before concluding tasks:
```sh
uv run pyrefly check                          # Must be 0 errors
uv run python -m unittest discover -s tests   # All tests green
graphify update .                             # Refresh knowledge graph
```

## Privacy & Sensitive Data Protection
- `data/` directory contains real customer network state and is gitignored.
- NEVER write real device models, software versions, real IPs, hostnames, serial numbers, or MACs into tracked files or comments.
- ALWAYS use RFC 5737 example data (`192.0.2.x`, `198.51.100.x`), placeholder hostnames (`switch-01`), and sample MACs (`AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF`).

## Knowledge Graph Navigation
- Query knowledge graph before deep source scanning:
```sh
uv run graphify query "<question>"
uv run graphify path "<nodeA>" "<nodeB>"
uv run graphify explain "<concept>"
```
- After code changes, run `graphify update .` to update graphify output.

## Coding Style & Architecture
- Keep simple solutions; do not add unrequested abstractions or feature flags.
- Maintain existing API contracts and type annotations.
